MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stage 3 of the audio roadmap, no new dependencies:

- resample: linear, cubic and Kaiser-windowed-sinc polyphase conversion,
  one-shot (Samples::resampled, time-aligned) or streaming in any chunk
  size with identical output; support widens with the downsampling ratio.
  997 Hz at 44.1→48 kHz leaves a residual under −100 dB; a 10 kHz tone
  taken to 16 kHz is removed to below −80 dB rather than folding.
  MixError::RateMismatch now names the explicit fix.
- channels: mono/stereo/quad/5.1/7.1/discrete layouts in WAV order with
  Web Audio's speaker up/down-mix tables, extended to 7.1 per BS.775
- automation: Web Audio AudioParam timeline (set, linear, exponential,
  setTarget, value curves, cancel, cancel-and-hold) as a pure function of
  time; DAW lanes in beats with linear/exp/smooth/step/tension segments and
  Ramer–Douglas–Peucker thinning for recorded controller moves
- graph: Web Audio-style node graph — sources, buffers, processors, stereo
  effects, automated gains (buses), sends with per-connection gain,
  panners, closures; channel remixing on every edge; cycles only through
  DelayNode, with the block of latency subtracted so delay time stays
  exact. A counting-allocator test proves the render path allocates
  nothing.
- stream: lock-free SPSC ring from atomics (no unsafe), a render thread
  that keeps it topped up, device-side pull with underrun accounting
- transport: tempo maps with steps and closed-form exact ramps,
  time-signature changes, bars/beats/ticks at 960 PPQ, looping, a
  sample-accurate scheduler with sub-sample fractions and in-block loop
  wrap, 24-ppq MIDI clock-out positions
- fx::delay: tempo-synced stereo/ping-pong delay with filtered feedback
  and gliding time changes

233 unit tests + allocation test, clippy clean.

