Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stage 4 of the audio roadmap, no new dependencies:

- synth::granular: fixed-pool grain clouds (no allocation while
  rendering), synchronous or Poisson scheduling, Hann/Gauss/Tukey/
  trapezoid windows, position/pitch/pan scatter, reverse grains, and
  independent scan speed and pitch — time-stretch and pitch-shift
- synth::physical: Karplus–Strong with all-pass fine tuning (within 3
  cents from 110 Hz to 1.3 kHz), circular pluck-position comb, T60 decay
  and brightness; STK-style clarinet (reed table) and bowed string
  (stick-slip bow table) waveguides with breath/bow pressure; modal bars
  (marimba, glockenspiel, wood) with mallet hardness; a mass–spring chain
  on its analytic first mode. All are polyphony Voices.
- synth::sampler: key/velocity zones, cubic repitching, forward/
  ping-pong/sustain/one-shot loops with crossfades, round robin,
  keyswitches, release triggers, choke groups, pedal, pitch bend
- synth::sfz: SFZ with header inheritance, note names, control offsets,
  and the mapping/tuning/loop/round-robin/keyswitch/trigger/group/ampeg
  opcodes; unknown opcodes reported, not dropped
- synth::sf2: SoundFont 2 (16- and 24-bit) with global zones, additive
  preset generators, intersecting ranges, timecent/centibel conversion,
  exclusive classes; SF3's compressed samples route to codec::vorbis,
  whose decoder lands in the next stage

267 unit tests, clippy clean.

