Stage 5 of the audio roadmap. Every codec is written here; three take only
their standards' fixed tables from permissively licensed references
(tools/THIRD_PARTY.md). Each decoder is graded against ffmpeg's own decode
of a file made by an independent encoder (tests/fixtures/make.sh):

- WAV: 8/16/24/32-bit integer and 32/64-bit float, WAVE_FORMAT_EXTENSIBLE
  with channel masks, any layout (read_wav_multi / write_wav_format)
- AIFF/AIFF-C: read NONE/twos/sowt/fl32/fl64, write 16/24-bit; 80-bit
  extended rates
- FLAC: full decoder (all subframes, wasted bits, Rice/Rice2, every stereo
  mode) verifying CRC-8, CRC-16 and the stream MD5 — ffmpeg's 16- and
  24-bit files decode bit-exactly; encoder (fixed + LPC to order 12,
  partition search, stereo-mode search) that ffmpeg decodes bit-exactly,
  within 10% of `-compression_level 8`
- MP3: MPEG-1/2/2.5 Layer III with bit reservoir, LSF scalefactors,
  MS/intensity stereo, mixed blocks, LAME gapless — 88.8 dB (joint stereo
  CBR) and 86.3 dB (mono VBR) SNR against ffmpeg, sample-aligned
- Ogg/Vorbis: page CRCs, floor 0/1, residue 0/1/2, coupling, granule
  trimming — 89.0 dB, exact length
- AAC-LC: ADTS and MP4 (sample tables, esds, edit lists), M/S, intensity,
  PNS, TNS, pulse data, KBD/sine windows — 89.3 dB (ADTS) and 89.2 dB (M4A,
  priming and padding trimmed); PNS bands within 0.13 dB of the
  reference's band energy
- SF3 SoundFonts now decode their Vorbis samples
- fft::Imdct shared by Vorbis and AAC, checked against its definition
- midi: QuarterFrame/SongSelect/TuneRequest messages, SMF type 2 per-pattern
  tempo, SMPTE time division, clip export (Smf::from_notes), ClockIn tempo
  follower, MIDI Time Code with drop-frame, quarter- and full-frame I/O
- midi_io: live input over any byte stream (ALSA rawmidi on Linux) with
  arrival timestamps, output to any sink, device enumeration

316 unit tests + allocation test, clippy clean.

