From e6f6f5b11f3975a39f7b3e49c5a8ceca4652cabd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:36:21 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] =?UTF-8?q?vieww-audio:=20device=20backends=20for=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?every=20platform=20=E2=80=94=20PipeWire,=20JACK,=20PulseAudio,?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20ALSA,=20Core=20Audio,=20WASAPI,=20AAudio,=20Web=20Audio?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

One callback interface (backend::Backend: open_output/open_input with
interleaved f32 render/capture callbacks, the granted configuration,
callback/frame/xrun counters, stop on drop) and a default chain that takes
the first available system. Every system is reached through the library
the platform ships, loaded at run time or linked as a system framework —
no binding crates, so the crate keeps its single dependency.

- PipeWire: native pw_stream on a pw_thread_loop; the SPA format POD is
  encoded here and tested byte-for-byte against spa_format_audio_raw_build;
  the RT process callback renders into the dequeued buffer.
- JACK: real-time process callback over per-channel ports, chunked
  interleaved scratch (no allocation on the RT thread), xrun/shutdown
  callbacks, auto-connection to physical ports.
- PulseAudio: the simple API with server-paced blocking writes/reads.
- ALSA: stream threads over the raw-kernel PCM, now with capture (READI).
- Core Audio: DefaultOutput / HALOutput Audio Units, float stream format,
  render and input callbacks.
- WASAPI: event-driven shared mode with engine format conversion; vtables,
  GUIDs and WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE checked against the Windows SDK headers.
- AAudio: low-latency data-callback streams via libaaudio.so.
- Web Audio: raw wasm imports plus web/vieww-audio.js (AudioWorklet with a
  demand-driven block queue), tested under Node with a simulated browser.

Tested here against live servers (jackd dummy driver, PulseAudio null sink,
PipeWire + WirePlumber null sink) with VIEWW_EXPECT_BACKENDS making
"unavailable" a failure; the other platforms type-check and lint on Linux
via --cfg vieww_check_all, and a CI workflow runs each on its platform.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
