From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:58:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] Metal and D3D12 render paths, a cross-platform
 type-check from Linux, and the framework-checks workflow
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The two GPU backends that were device bring-up only now render:

- vieww-hal::metal: render_clear_to_pixels and render_mesh_to_pixels on
  macOS and iOS, through the same solid.wgsl the Vulkan path uses, compiled
  WGSL -> MSL -> newLibraryWithSource. Private render target, blit to a
  Shared buffer for readback (correct on Intel, Apple silicon and iOS).
- vieww-hal::d3d12: the same pair on Windows: HLSL from naga compiled with
  d3dcompiler_47 (SM 5.1), root constants at b0 for the uniform, a fenced
  readback through a 256-byte-pitched buffer, and an opt-in WARP fallback
  (VIEWW_D3D12_ALLOW_WARP=1) so GPU-less CI runners can run it.
- tests/metal_smoke.rs, tests/d3d12_smoke.rs: the Vulkan smoke suites'
  claims (exact clear, unmirrored mesh, pixel rule, empty mesh, refused bad
  index, repeated frames); VIEWW_REQUIRE_HARDWARE=gpu makes a missing
  device fail instead of skip.

vieww-shaders::to_msl emitted naga's `[[user(fake0)]]` placeholder
bindings, which no Metal compiler accepts; it now binds every resource to a
real slot under a documented convention (msl_slots / hlsl_slots). Every
built-in shader's HLSL was compiled with DXC on Linux: all 22 entry points
compile.

ci/check/cross-check.sh type-checks the whole workspace, every target, for
aarch64-apple-darwin, aarch64-apple-ios, x86_64-pc-windows-msvc and
aarch64-linux-android from a Linux machine with none of those SDKs: std is
built from source (-Zbuild-std), and stub cc/ar/xcrun stand in for the C
toolchains a type-check never links with. Its first run found real bugs,
all fixed here:

- vieww-audio-plugin assumed c_char is i8 (it is u8 on Android/arm64 Linux)
- vieww-audio on Windows: an unused import; on iOS: no backend at all and
  dead dlopen code. The Core Audio backend now drives RemoteIO on iOS.
- examples/reload-android had drifted from Reloader::root's Result API
- vieww-platform-winit's desktop example did not build for Android

.github/workflows/framework-checks.yml (described in TRACKER.md but never
committed — the earlier push lacked workflow scope): checks.sh, coverage,
the cross type-check, Vulkan suites on lavapipe plus a GPU frame presented
to an Xvfb window, macOS + iOS with the Metal suite, Windows with the D3D12
suite on WARP, Android, web canvas parity in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit
(verify_web.py now takes VIEWW_WEB_BROWSER), and an on-demand self-hosted
Android device leg.

Verified here: the GPU window scenario on lavapipe (5/5), the cross
type-check on all four targets, clippy -D warnings for vieww-hal's Metal
and D3D12 code on their own targets.

