Applied the supplied "rechecked" gap-closure patch's new crate and its
workspace wiring. As supplied it did not compile — `i128::from(isize)` has
no impl — and failed `clippy -D warnings` on six sites; both fixed, and the
crate is rustfmt'd to the workspace style. 39 unit tests + 1 doctest pass.

Not applied from that patch: its edits to Cargo.lock, README.md,
crates/vieww/src/lib.rs's doc and PENDING.md, which were made against an
older snapshot and no longer apply; the facade gets only the
`pub use vieww_spatial as spatial` re-export.

PENDING §1.2/§1.3 rewritten: Metal and D3D12 now have render paths that
are type-checked and linted on their own targets but have never executed.

