Subject: [PATCH 11/15] GPU: antialias every non-analytic shape with the CPU
 rasterizer's own coverage
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rotated rects, arbitrary fills and all strokes used to tessellate and
rasterise with hard edges on the GPU — PENDING §2.1. They now draw as one
quad over their inked pixels, sampling an R8 coverage patch that
GpuSeam::shape_coverage computes with NativeRenderer's own polygon
construction, flattening and 4x4 coverage, placed in the mask atlas
(cached by content; any shaped clip multiplied in; patches over ~1.4 Mpx
fall back to tessellation instead of claiming the atlas).

Census on lavapipe, before -> after: worst channel 203 -> 47/255; channels
over 1/255 525,299 -> 245,647; fixtures with interior mismatches 6 -> 2.

vulkan_scene gains a test holding a rotated rect, a star, a dashed curve
and a clipped circle within 2/255 on every pixel; disabling the change
makes it fail at 180/255. Planner tests cover the clip product, the
cache hit and the oversize fallback. The stroke's gradient box now uses
the CPU's own inflation.

PENDING §2.1 now records the residual: a path that changes every frame is
re-rasterised on the CPU every frame.

