From cecb86ee88fcdc07fe152f97b59212ad3ae64ca3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:04:45 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] GPU window path: render straight into the swapchain
 image, no readback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PENDING §2.2. NativeRenderer::present_planned used to render the plan,
read the frame back into host memory, unpremultiply and quantise it on the
CPU, and upload it again through the swapchain's staging buffer. For an
opaque frame it now acquires the swapchain image and
SceneRenderer::render_planned_to blits the RGBA16F frame target straight
into it (vkCmdBlitImage converts to the swapchain's UNORM format and BGRA
order), waiting on the acquire semaphore only at the blit stage.

- vieww-hal swapchain: AcquiredImage, acquire_image, present_acquired,
  abandon_acquired (an image acquired and never presented would eventually
  block acquisition forever), can_blit_scene_frames (asks the driver for
  BLIT_SRC/BLIT_DST rather than trusting the spec's mandatory table).
- A translucent window, or a driver without blit support, keeps the
  readback path. FrameReport::gpu_direct_frames counts which ran.

wait_loop's gpu_frame scenario now asserts every GPU frame went direct and
grabs the Xvfb screen to check the window shows its colour; with the blit
disabled it fails with 0 blue pixels.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nd3Ehrf9ktGu82K38kGEjH
