From c1f15c3bd21ae0915f59dac95fc1e53ffa5dab35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:19:07 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] viewwsite: light colour scheme and keyboard reach; DOM
 backend colour tokens and button semantics
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The site README listed three gaps. Checked against the code:

- Device-pixel scale was already closed (WebSurface::resize); README fixed.
- Keyboard: the DOM page's controls are links in document order, but the
  install section's "Copy" control was a div with a script click
  listener — unreachable by Tab. It is now a <button>. More generally,
  vieww-platform-web-dom gave any GestureDetector a click listener and
  nothing else; non-button tap targets now get tabindex=0, role=button
  and Enter/Space.
- prefers-color-scheme: vieww_platform_web_dom::set_color_tokens maps
  palette colours to CSS custom properties (exact matches only; the tree
  stays literal and still rasterises). The site registers its palette and
  index.html gains a light block; glass/border washes go through a
  --glass channel variable. Code panels, terminal and phone stay dark.

Also VNode::to_html and an examples/snapshot.rs that writes the page as
static HTML without wasm. Verified in Chromium with emulated schemes:
backgrounds rgb(15,13,11) / rgb(251,249,247), Copy reached by Tab in both.

The wasm build lints clean again: fixed a drop_non_drop in vieww-video's
export and a vec_init_then_push in vieww-audio's backend list, both
wasm-only and pre-existing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nd3Ehrf9ktGu82K38kGEjH
