From 8dc90b52059a78763548ccc992c73512010533e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:20:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] Refresh rate: re-read it when a window changes monitor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PENDING §3.2 said the platform's refresh rate is never read. Checked
against winit 0.30.13's source: winit reports it on macOS, iOS, Windows,
X11 and Wayland, and this crate already reads Android's below winit. The
real gap was timing — it was read only when a window opened, so a window
dragged from a 60Hz display to a 144Hz one kept a 16.7ms budget, and a
Wayland surface that had not entered an output at open kept the default.

WindowState now remembers the monitor the rate came from and re-reads it
on Moved and ScaleFactorChanged when that monitor changed. Not exercised
with a real second monitor (Xvfb has one CRTC); PENDING §3.2 says so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nd3Ehrf9ktGu82K38kGEjH
