From 731633cb87701b4be99812776b6327fcd9907e0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:47:26 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] viewwstudio: out-of-process preview (child process per
 Render)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PENDING §3.3. src/remote.rs: a small length-prefixed protocol over the
child's pipes, RemotePreview (host handle; child death becomes
RemoteError::Crashed with the guest's stderr), RemoteHandle, and the
child's serve loop, which loads the cdylib with loaded::Preview::load and
draws it under the same ui::preview::guest_tree the in-process pane uses
(extracted so both match). New binary viewwstudio-preview. The pane's
RemoteScreen shows the child's frames, forwards press/move/release, and
keeps asking while the guest animates. Setting "Run preview in its own
process", default on Windows; ABI mismatches feed the studio's existing
candidate walk.

tests/remote.rs (4/4 on Linux): frames, taps, 2x, state across an
environment change; a guest abort kills only the child; a later-rebuild
panic is survived; the studio's own Render goes to a child and the pane
requests frames. Clippy clean. Not yet: key/scroll/hover forwarding,
remote state capture, a Windows run, a full viewwstudio suite re-run.

TODO.md lists the remaining work.

